hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2712","Narrated to us Salamah ibn Shaybah, who said: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn 'Awn narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:
""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) faced the Black Stone, then he touched it and placed his lips upon it for a long time, weeping. I turned around and saw 'Umar (RA) weeping. So he said: 'O 'Umar, this is where tears are shed.'""

**CHAPTER:**"
"2713","###
 Narrated to us Muhammad bin Yahya, who said: Narrated to us Nu'aym bin Hammad, who said: Narrated to us Isa bin Yunus, who said: Narrated to us Muhammad bin Ishaq, from Abu Ja'far, who is Muhammad bin Ali, from Jabir bin Abdullah (RA), who said: ""We entered Makkah when the sun had risen high (Dhuha time). The Prophet (ﷺ) came to the door of the Masjid, alighted from his mount, and then entered the"
